# GDScript Standards

## Language rules
- Use Godot 4.x GDScript syntax ONLY. Never suggest C#.
- Always use static typing: `var x: int = 0`, `func foo(bar: String) -> void:`
- Use `class_name` for reusable classes
- Prefer `@export` for inspector-editable values
- Use `const` for values that never change at runtime
- Use `enum` for named states (e.g. `enum GamePhase { SETUP, PLAYING, PAYOUT }`)

## Signal conventions
- ALL cross-node communication goes through `SignalBus` autoload
- Never use `get_node()` or `$NodePath` to call methods on other scenes
- Local signals (within one scene) are fine to declare and emit directly
- Signal names: snake_case verbs — `sphere_hit_element`, `quota_paid`

## File & class structure
- One class per file
- Order: class_name → extends → signals → enums → constants → @export vars →
  regular vars → _ready() → _process() → public methods → private methods
- Private methods: prefix with underscore `_calculate_penalty()`
- No logic in _ready() beyond node reference caching and signal connections

## Node references
- Cache node refs in _ready() using @onready:
  `@onready var _win_bank: WinBank = $WinBank`
- Never use find_child() or get_node() with long paths

## Comments
- Write comments in RUSSIAN (matching the project language)
- Comment WHY, not WHAT
- Every exported variable needs a comment explaining its purpose

## Error handling
- Always validate inputs: `assert(amount > 0, "Сумма должна быть положительной")`
- Use `push_error()` for recoverable errors, `assert()` for programming errors

## Performance
- Never create objects in _process() — pool or pre-instantiate
- Use `call_deferred()` when modifying scene tree during physics callbacks